# Prototype UI Constraints

This project is a wireframe-level HTML prototype. The client should focus on structure and
content, not visual design. Visual design comes in a later phase.

## No colour

Only black, white, and greys. Every colour value must come from the greyscale tokens in
`assets/css/styles.css`.

```css
/* BAD */
background: #6f2da8;
border-color: rgb(0 120 255);

/* GOOD */
background: var(--c-surface);
border-color: var(--c-line);
```

All images, logos, and video posters must render greyscale:

```css
img, svg, video { filter: grayscale(100%); }
```

## Everything square

No rounded corners anywhere: buttons, cards, inputs, modals, avatars, badges, images.
`border-radius` must always be `0`. No drop shadows — use 1px borders (`var(--c-line)`) for
separation.

## Minimal type scale

Use only the text classes defined in `assets/css/styles.css` (8–12 total, e.g. `.t-display`,
`.t-h1`, `.t-h2`, `.t-h3`, `.t-lead`, `.t-body`, `.t-small`, `.t-label`). Do not introduce new
`font-size`, `font-weight`, or `line-height` declarations in page or component CSS — extend the
scale in `styles.css` instead, and only if nothing existing fits.

## Placeholders over assets

Real photos are not needed. Use the `.ph` placeholder block (grey box with a label) for imagery.
